.9402005929477071,"_gp_net_debt_ebitda":true,"_score_net_debt_ebitda":68.0,"_gate_accruals":0.01041259081110045,"_gp_accruals":true,"_score_accruals":11.1,"_gate_rev_volatility":0.19542861536302814,"_gp_rev_volatility":false,"_score_rev_volatility":58.4,"_gate_margin_vs_hist":0.04020730277581796,"_gp_margin_vs_hist":true,"_score_margin_vs_hist":49.7,"_gate_piotroski":5,"_gp_piotroski":false,"_score_piotroski":55.6,"_gate_spread":-0.038677364291690636,"_gp_spread":false,"_score_spread":0.0,"_gate_roic_consistency":6.617291261762767,"_gp_roic_consistency":false,"_score_roic_consistency":0.0,"_gate_incr_roic":0.16231032365581965,"_gp_incr_roic":true,"_score_incr_roic":70.8,"_gate_margin_advantage":-0.04157581699564414,"_gp_margin_advantage":false,"_score_margin_advantage":19.5,"_gate_pool_share":null,"_gp_pool_share":null,"_score_pool_share":null,"_gate_rev_durability":0.08652253817708377,"_gp_rev_durability":true,"_score_rev_durability":68.3,"_gate_fcf_durability":0.347979692757731,"_gp_fcf_durability":true,"_score_fcf_durability":100.0,"_gate_margins":-0.002481778647440025,"_gp_margins":false,"_score_margins":47.5,"_gate_fund_growth":0.055029079084623705,"_gp_fund_growth":true,"_score_fund_growth":55.0,"_gate_shrhldr_yield":0.006518639257305326,"_gp_shrhldr_yield":false,"_score_shrhldr_yield":18.4,"_gate_share_shrink":0.011105201329622894,"_gp_share_shrink":false,"_score_share_shrink":36.1,"_gate_sbc_dilution":null,"_gp_sbc_dilution":null,"_score_sbc_dilution":0.0,"_gate_insider_own":0.21090001,"_gp_insider_own":true,"_score_insider_own":100.0,"_gate_insider_buying":null,"_gp_insider_buying":null,"_score_insider_buying":null,"pf":[],"description_full":"Twin Disc, Incorporated engages in the design, manufacture, and sale of marine and heavy duty off-highway power transmission equipment in the United States, the Netherlands, China, Australia, Finland, Italy, and internationally. The company operates in two segments, Manufacturing and Distribution. It offers marine transmissions, azimuth drives, surface drives, propellers, and boat management systems, as well as power-shift transmissions, hydraulic torque converters, power take-offs, industrial clutches, controls systems, and braking systems. The company also provides third-party manufactured products. It sells its products through a direct sales force and distributor network to customers primarily in the pleasure craft, commercial, and military marine markets, as well as the energy and natural resources, government, military, and industrial markets. The company was incorporated in 1918 and is headquartered in Milwaukee, Wisconsin.","ceo_bio":"Mr. John H. Batten | President, CEO & Director | Age 60 | Compensation: $1.3M (FY2026)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 1K people. Revenue per employee of $351K ranks in the below the sector median among Industrials peers. Each employee generates $8K of free cash flow annually. CEO compensation is 4\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags moderate compensation governance risk (4/10).","financial_summary":["Twin Disc, Incorporated is a small-cap industrials business with a $351M market cap on $381M of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +11% over the past three years and +9% annually across the full decade, a respectable pace for a business of this size.","Returns on capital run at 6% against a 9% cost of capital, which means the business is destroying value with every dollar it reinvests, with gross margins sitting at 28%.","The business throws off $9M in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 2 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders, with adequate 0.85\u00d7 cash conversion.","On the balance sheet, leverage is comfortably conservative at 0.9\u00d7 net debt/EBITDA, and interest coverage runs at 5.8\u00d7.","Shareholder yield is only 0.7%, a thin return of capital, and insiders hold 21% of the shares, so management thinks like owners because it is one \u2014 the strongest alignment there is, and profit capture is only 0.4\u00d7 the fair share, suggesting no structural edge inside its industry."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Price sits 33% above estimated fair value \u2014 no margin of safety left, and the cushion against estimate error has been bid away","sev":"red","cat":"valuation","magnitude":0.33449320629973406},{"text":"Fragmented industry with below-average profit capture \u2014 no moat to protect margins","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Volatile returns on capital suggest the moat is narrower than a snapshot ROIC implies","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Insiders are overwhelmingly selling (100% sell ratio) \u2014 the people who know the business want less of it","sev":"amber","cat":"insider","ratio":0.0},{"text":"Industrials sector lagging the market significantly, underperforming by 6% over 3 months","sev":"amber","cat":"sector"},{"text":"Cyclicality and capital intensity \u2014 order books turn on a dime, and the heavy fixed cost base that creates the moat also magnifies the downturn.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Supply chain reshoring costs and labour shortages \u2014 onshoring mandates raise capex requirements while a shrinking skilled-labour pool inflates operating costs.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Tariff and trade-policy exposure \u2014 industrial exporters sit squarely in the crosshairs of protectionist policy, and retaliatory tariffs can close markets without warning.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Healthy payout ratio leaves room for both dividend growth and reinvestment","Minimal goodwill on the balance sheet \u2014 low impairment risk"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"Twin Disc, Incorporated (NASDAQ:TWIN) Looks Interesting, And It's About To Pay A Dividend","source":"simplywall.st","link":"https://simplywall.st/stocks/us/capital-goods/nasdaq-twin/twin-disc/news/twin-disc-incorporated-nas